erted troubleshooting mutations were identified. The restart protocol is strong: the pre-restart boot ID and working render were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, the system recovered to running state, and the application, template, OS, and kernel were revalidated; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree. Hygiene is reduced because evidence artifacts were left behind: /tmp/render-verify.31Wevi with requested-report.txt and /tmp/render-restart-baseline.out remained, and /var/tmp/render-after-reboot.out was created without demonstrated cleanup. System services, sockets, and package health otherwise remained healthy; socket differences are only post-reboot process descriptors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eec2b3c81bac4c0e","cmd-e1498dd0dc2e4056","cmd-2fa347c23f0241c2","cmd-7ad150349440483c","cmd-2492130085b14d6a","cmd-1437296706d44e95","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence, including persistence across the mandatory node restart. The only notable deficiency is minor retained verification-output residue.","limitations":["Lifecycle file inventory is bounded to /tmp, so it does not independently confirm cleanup or retention of the directly observed /var/tmp/render-after-reboot.out.","The evidence demonstrates operation from multiple unrelated working directories rather than literally every possible directory, which is a reasonable behavioral test of the self-locating implementation."]}
